{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"code-critique","packet_sha256":"cfa9d1df9c760397727138ae63ba2e0dea135c1298b73b2a6c0fc082d01d6df0","reviewed_input_identity_sha256":"b91f6a6092bd04d4f8e3333a8d354bce2c4662aa9f4d5acb5bae4435c0f9b937","verdict":"block","target_observations":[{"target":"docs/agent-task-runs.md","verdict":"pass","summary":"The documentation describes independent no-progress and blocked-linger configuration consistently with ordinary finite values.","evidence":["The page documents `CHARNESS_TASK_RUN_NO_PROGRESS_SECONDS` and `CHARNESS_TASK_RUN_BLOCKED_GRACE_SECONDS`, including their non-positive disable behavior.","It identifies `stop_enabled` and `linger_stop_enabled` as separate receipt fields."]},{"target":"scripts/task_run/task_run_progress.py","verdict":"block","summary":"Non-finite environment values bypass validation and can make receipt configuration contradict actual stop behavior.","evidence":["`_env_seconds` accepts any value parsed by `float(...)`; Python accepts `nan`, `inf`, and `-inf` without raising `ValueError`.","For a NaN no-progress budget, `receipt()` reports `stop_enabled: false` because `nan > 0` is false, while `no_progress_stop_due()` does not disable the stop because `nan <= 0` is also false; its elapsed comparison is false, so an eligible lane is stopped immediately.","For a NaN blocked grace, `receipt()` similarly reports `linger_stop_enabled: false`, but `tick()` neither takes the `<= 0` disabled branch nor the `< grace` waiting branch, causing a lingering blocked lane to stop on the next poll."]},{"target":"tests/charness_cli/test_task_run_implementation_lane.py","verdict":"block","summary":"Tests cover non-numeric fallback and ordinary/non-positive values, but omit non-finite values that expose the configuration/receipt inconsistency.","evidence":["`test_invalid_budget_env_falls_back_to_default` covers only `not-a-number`.","No test supplies `nan`, `inf`, or `-inf` for either duration environment variable.","Existing receipt-independence tests therefore do not verify that the enabled flags match runtime behavior for every value accepted by `_env_seconds`."]}],"findings":[{"id":"linger-config-nonfinite-values","severity":"medium","summary":"NaN duration configuration can activate immediate stopping while the receipt says that stop mechanism is disabled.","evidence":["`_env_seconds` returns `float(os.environ.get(name, default))` and rejects only conversion exceptions, not non-finite results.","IEEE NaN makes both `value > 0` and `value <= 0` false, splitting the receipt predicate from the runtime disable predicate.","The same defect affects both the no-progress budget and blocked-linger grace, despite their intended independent configuration."],"action":"Reject non-finite parsed durations (for example with `math.isfinite`) and fall back to the documented default, then add tests for non-finite values for both environment variables and assert receipt flags agree with `tick()` behavior."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"Accepting positive infinity could intentionally mean an effectively unlimited wait.","bin":"non-blocking design choice","disposition":"Infinity semantics may be chosen explicitly, but they should not arise accidentally from the current generic float parser; the blocking defect is the demonstrably contradictory NaN behavior."},{"concern":"The receipt has only one `stop_reason` rather than separate outcome fields for the two mechanisms.","bin":"not established as defect","disposition":"Only one watch stop can win for a single execution, and the reason text distinguishes the observed cause; the packet does not establish a consumer requiring two simultaneous outcome fields."},{"concern":"An empty `BLOCKED:` marker is ignored.","bin":"low-priority protocol enforcement","disposition":"The documented protocol requires `BLOCKED: <reason>`, so ignoring an empty declaration is defensible and does not block this slice."}],"next_move":"Harden duration parsing against non-finite floats and add focused budget/grace tests proving that receipt enablement fields and live stopping use identical effective configuration semantics.","non_claims":["No workspace files were inspected or modified; the review used only the identity-bound inline payload.","No claim is made that the supplied tests were executed.","No approval is inferred from the committed-ref packet or its validation metadata.","Goal evidence lineage is not goal-bound, as explicitly recorded in the packet."]}
